{"lines": ["At 2:10 in the afternoon, five Avenger torpedo bombers left Fort Lauderdale, Florida, on a training flight called Flight 19.", "Fourteen men were aboard, led by an instructor, Lieutenant Charles Taylor.", "They dropped their practice bombs, and then something went wrong.", "Taylor radioed, \"Both of my compasses are out,\" and said he was sure he was over the Florida Keys.", "But he was actually over the Bahamas, so instead of heading home, he led them farther out to sea.", "One voice in the flight said if they could just fly west, they would get home.", "Then the weather turned, and the sun went down.", "Taylor's last message came after dark: \"When the first plane drops below ten gallons, we all go down together.\"", "Then the rescue flying boat took off, with thirteen men.", "Later that night, a tanker saw flames leap a hundred feet high, then found only oil and gasoline on the water.", "The Navy first blamed Taylor, but later changed its verdict to \"cause unknown.\"", "Planes can vanish in a storm, but the next one was a 465-foot passenger liner."], "words": [["At", 0.0, 0.12], ["2:10", 0.12, 0.96], ["in", 0.96, 1.22], ["the", 1.22, 1.3], ["afternoon,", 1.3, 1.64], ["five", 2.26, 2.62], ["Avenger", 2.62, 3.0], ["torpedo", 3.0, 3.34], ["bombers", 3.34, 3.96], ["left", 3.96, 4.34], ["Fort", 4.34, 4.7], ["Lauderdale,", 4.7, 5.1], ["Florida,", 5.56, 5.72], ["on", 6.28, 6.44], ["a", 6.44, 6.52], ["training", 6.52, 6.74], ["flight", 6.74, 7.18], ["called", 7.18, 7.62], ["Flight", 7.62, 7.88], ["19.", 7.88, 8.36], ["Fourteen", 9.0, 9.36], ["men", 9.36, 9.62], ["were", 9.62, 9.84], ["aboard,", 9.84, 10.06], ["led", 10.66, 10.76], ["by", 10.76, 11.02], ["an", 11.02, 11.12], ["instructor,", 11.12, 11.52], ["Lieutenant", 12.2, 12.3], ["Charles", 12.3, 13.04], ["Taylor.", 13.04, 13.36], ["They", 14.04, 14.12], ["dropped", 14.12, 14.36], ["their", 14.36, 14.66], ["practice", 14.66, 15.0], ["bombs,", 15.0, 15.28], ["and", 15.98, 16.03], ["then", 16.03, 16.1], ["s